TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (CaddG) and add the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  For the mandolin opening of the intro begin by forming (D) but add your pinky to the 1st string of the 3rd fret so you get (Dsus4).  Now pick the covered 1st string <g>, lift off the pinky and pick the still covered 1st string <f#> and strum (G).  (Notes may or may not transpose.)  This may seem counterintuitive but if you do it this way you'll be set up for the second time around in which it comes off a (D).  And later in the song there's a (D) (Dsus4) (D) voicing after the verse.

{c: TIP:  When playing through the instrumental bridge that leads into the setup (E) for the key change, it may help to think of (Esus) as an (A) played up one string-set when coming off the preceding (C), rather than fumbling around with your pinky after hitting the (E) and then looking for the (Esus).  And chords in |brackets| means strum just once at that position.
  

